GameEngine overlay patch for yoga 3.2.1.

algorithm: resolve flexible lengths by the CSS Flexbox 9.7 freeze loop.

Yoga resolves flexible lengths in two fixed passes and says so in the comment
above resolveFlexibleLength: "This two pass approach for resolving min/max
constraints deviates from the spec ... The algorithm implemented here won't
handle all cases but it was simpler to implement". Two things go wrong, both
because distribution starts from the MIN/MAX-CLAMPED basis rather than the flex
base size:

  distributeFreeSpaceFirstPass freezes an item only when its distributed size
  differs from its clamped size. Starting from a min-clamped basis, min + share
  is already >= min, so the two are equal, the item never freezes, and it grows
  ON TOP of its minimum. Three flex:1 1 0 items in a 400px row, the first with
  min-width:200, lay out 266.67 / 66.67 / 66.67 where CSS and every browser give
  200 / 100 / 100.

  calculateFlexLine (FlexLine.cpp) accumulates sizeConsumed from clamped bases
  but totalFlexShrinkScaledFactors from unclamped ones, so under shrink the
  shortfall is measured against one denominator and shared out against another.
  Three flex-basis:200px shrink:1 items in a 300px row, the first with
  max-width:90, lay out 61.5 / 136.67 / 136.67 -- summing to 334.83 inside a
  300px box -- where CSS gives 90 / 105 / 105.

This replaces both passes with the spec loop
(https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS-flexbox-1/#resolve-flexible-lengths): size the
inflexible items, then repeatedly distribute the free space over the unfrozen
items FROM THEIR FLEX BASE SIZES, clamp, and freeze the items violating in the
same direction as the line's total violation, until nothing freezes. The number
of distributions is data-dependent, which is the point: an item can come into
violation only after a sibling has frozen, and the sign rule leaves a
min-violating item flexible while the line as a whole is over-full.

totalFlexShrinkScaledFactors becomes dead once the loop computes its own
per-distribution sums, and so does the floor-to-1 on totalFlexGrowFactors, whose
one remaining reader only tests it against zero. Both are removed rather than
left to rot.

Verified against Chrome 150.0.7871.186 (--headless=new, --force-device-scale-factor
1 and 2) on both divergences above, their x8 variants, the column-axis variant, a
four-item cascade needing three distributions (300 / 150 / 75 / 75) and a line
carrying violations of both signs (30 / 90 / 90 / 90). Yoga's own test corpus is
unchanged by this patch: with every GTEST_SKIP removed, stock and patched both
run 784 tests with the same 771 passing and the same 13 failing.

Two of those 13 are min_width and min_height, which upstream skips. They are NOT
fixed by this patch and are a separate defect: for flex-basis:auto items whose
main-size property is also auto, computeFlexBasisForChild takes the child's
MEASURED main dimension as the flex base size, and measurement has already
applied that child's own min/max. The flex base size arrives pre-clamped, so the
loop above cannot tell it from a hypothetical size. Items with an explicit
flex-basis, or with a definite main-size property, are unaffected.

When upstream vcpkg bumps the yoga version, resync this portfile and vcpkg.json
and re-cut this patch against the new source (cut it against the
disable_tests-patched tree, since vcpkg applies patches in order).

